# LÖVE2D build artifacts
*.love

# Everything the icon pipeline vendors or stages. None of it is committed: it is a large
# third-party checkout plus a downloaded binary, all reproducible with tools/icons/fetch.ps1.
#
#   vendor/game-icons/  ~4200 CC BY 3.0 SVGs cloned from github.com/game-icons/icons
#   vendor/bin/         the pinned resvg rasterizer
#   vendor/staging/     colorized SVGs written on the way to a PNG
vendor/
*.resvg.tmp.svg

# Rendered/generated art is NOT committed (project decision). Item icons are reproducible from
# blueprint tags with `. icon-compose assets`; other buckets are provided locally. A fresh clone
# has no icons until the composer runs -- models/sprite.lua tolerates the gap (a missing file
# resolves to its path string rather than crashing). See docs/art-assets.md.
assets/

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor directories
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
*.swp
*.swo

# Logs
*.log

# Steam native binaries and the local app id. Not committed on purpose: they are large,
# platform-specific, and licensed separately (steam_api64.dll comes from the Steamworks SDK), and
# steam_appid.txt is a local development detail rather than a property of the game.
#
# The game runs perfectly well without them -- models/steam.lua reports "not available" with a
# reason, and asynchronous build PvP needs no Steam at all. See docs/multiplayer.md for where each
# one comes from.
luasteam.dll
luasteam.so
luasteam.dylib
steam_api.dll
steam_api64.dll
libsteam_api.so
libsteam_api.dylib
steam_appid.txt
